      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patients with low back pain without a sufficient physical cause attract labels such as \"hysteria\" and \"hypochondriasis,\" often on the basis of exclusion. The concept of \"abnormal illness behavior\" was introduced to clarify the classification and diagnosis of these conditions, in which the behavior of the doctor plays a particularly important part. Principles of management are discussed."},
